.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_FREE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_free
.Nd free an allocated SSL_CTX object
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_free
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CTX_free
decrements the reference count of
.Fa ctx ,
and removes the SSL_CTX object pointed to by
.Fa ctx
and frees up the allocated memory if the reference count has reached 0.
.Pp
It also calls the free()ing procedures for indirectly affected items, if
applicable: the session cache, the list of ciphers, the list of Client
CAs, the certificates and keys.
.Pp
If
.Fa ctx
is NULL nothing is done.
.Sh WARNINGS
If a session-remove callback is set
.Xr (SSL_CTX_sess_set_remove_cb 3 ) ,
this callback will be called for each session being freed from
.Fa ctx Ns 's
session cache.
This implies, that all corresponding sessions from an external session
cache are removed as well.
If this is not desired, the user should explicitly unset the callback by
calling
.Pf SSL_CTX_sess_set_remove_cb( Fa ctx ,
NULL) prior to calling
.Fn SSL_CTX_free .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_CTX_free
does not provide diagnostic information.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SSL_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_sess_set_get_cb 3
